# CTF-04 passive per-attempt matrix observation proposal

SOURCE-READY source only. This extends held CTF03 observer39eb and adds one
passive call immediately after original Construction.cc728, inside the actual
one-dimensional branch and its existing retry loop. No scientific statement,
branch, arithmetic, allocation, helper call or retry condition is changed.
Removing the new call and restoring the include returns held03 byte-exactly;
removing all five passive calls/include returns pinned Original d85937 exactly.

The old three preprocessing Snapshots, separate initial619 owner, four phase
counts, their callback bodies and existing binding mechanism are unchanged.
Matrix visits have separate ordered records/counters, not a fifth old phase.
The actual counter increments once per visit to the sole post728 callsite for
the bound whole construction call. No count is inferred from timestep/history.
The future helper associates that binding with its actual model/lane, whole-call
ordinal, construction array index/name and original LayerPoint membership.
The Capture pointers are identity checks, never serialized IDs or operands.

MatrixAttemptSnapshot copies actual ErrorsFound/DoCTFErrorReport, IsUsedCTF,
SourceSinkPresent/SolutionDimensions/TotLayers, local LayersInConstruct and
NumResLayers, rcmax, reset NodeSource/NodeUserTemp, current CTFTimeStep bits,
NumHistories, and actual caller TimeStepZone bits. Its active prefix separately
copies dl/rk/rho/cp/lr/ResLayer and Nodes/dx. It invents no merged material IDs,
capacitance, conductance, node count, identity, zero entries or other arithmetic.
Only the actual copied local prefix is observed; the fixed-array tail is never
an operand. Nonselected source/sink context, if reached at this 1D site, remains
captured context, not certification of the pure selected no-source algorithm.

The actual AMat and IdenMatrix owners must have allocated bounds1..rcmax for
both dimensions and exact rcmax*rcmax storage. Their complete values are copied
i1 outer/i2 inner, with actual i2-contiguous orientation: flat offset
(i1-1)*rcmax+(i2-1). Every zero/nonfinite/signed-zero object representation is
copied by memcpy; no class conversion or off-band/identity synthesis occurs.
BMat(3), CMat(2), DMat(2) retain their genuine compressed shapes and values.
Actual allocated bounds/size are observed separately; null means unallocated.
Dimensions and shape arithmetic are metadata checks, not scientific evaluation.

Construction638-648 allocates/zeros AMat and creates Iden once, before657.
B/CD are allocated3/2/2 by the actual constructor330-332; their values become
initialized only through the reached assembly661-728. The callback reads them
at that final assignment. Each retry reuses actual AMat/Iden and rewrites the
selected assembly, not fresh inferred buffers. Nodes/dx/rcmax were produced
once before initial619. Retry908-936 changes current timestep/history only.
No later returned timestep replaces the initial snapshot or an earlier visit.
AMat/Iden are deallocated1082-1089; copies are made while real owners/local
arrays are alive, then retained independently for future serialization.

The callback is noexcept and never writes scientific state, performs floating
arithmetic, invokes an engine/helper or does I/O. Unlike the old fixed snapshots,
observation-only vectors allocate to retain every actual visit without an
invented attempt bound. Any allocation/copy exception is caught. A failed
record append increments matrix_attempt_records_omitted; its actual ordinal is
also retained in typed first/last failure metadata. All retained records carry
their true visit ordinal, so any missing ordinal in1..actual_callback_count is
an explicit missing whole record, never a skipped optional event. Copy failure
clears partial dynamic buffers and keeps matrices_available false.

Identity/order/prefix/shape/copy/append failures set matrix_observer_failure,
increment typed failure-event counters and retain first/last failure association.
Per-record failure_kinds preserves every detected category on retained records.
Any such failure is required observation-integrity FAIL in future helpers/QA,
not an optional unavailable event or numerical PASS. Helpers must fail before
comparison if totals, retained ordinals, omitted count, copied shapes or these
flags disagree. A reached missing matrix on either/both sides fails. No fixed
attempt cap, silent truncation, fallback values or relaxed numeric policy exists.
Unreached unused/loading-error/allR/reverse routes remain distinct unavailable
context; a completed assembly visit does not prove later Exp/Inverse returned.

This package adds no helper, serializer, input cases, numeric freeze, QA/proof
framework, execution stage or canonical change. Future helpers must compile
the matching fresh TU/header/implementation together, not mix Capture layouts
or link an earlier observer implementation. Source policy still requires Root
approval and full other-author review before any build/first observation.
I authored the held pure CTF04 algorithm; this package does not independently
certify that algorithm or any scientific output. Root and an other-author peer
must review these passive boundaries. All card gates and future execution facts
remain pending; no outputs/results/weather/binaries were read here.
